{
  "format": 1,
  "note": "The locked build profiles of hearth_sink's ESP32 boards (planning/esp32-platform-profiles.md). tools/hearth/sink_profile.py is the only reader: `defaults` gives a build's SDKCONFIG_DEFAULTS, `verify` holds a configured build to its profile, `snapshot --write` records what a build resolved. A profile changes in a pull request that edits this file, the fragment or the Kconfig default, and carries a board run.",
  "watch": [
    "*STACK*",
    "*IN_PSRAM*",
    "ICLFORGE_EXAMPLE_*RING*",
    "ICLFORGE_EXAMPLE_I2S_DMA_*",
    "ICLFORGE_EXAMPLE_*_CORE",
    "ICLFORGE_EXAMPLE_PLAY_MIN_FREE_BYTES",
    "ICLFORGE_EXAMPLE_SENDSPIN_*",
    "ICLFORGE_EXAMPLE_DECODE_LANE",
    "ICLFORGE_EXAMPLE_AC4_*",
    "ICLFORGE_EXAMPLE_HOLD_FIRST_UNIT",
    "ICLFORGE_AC4*",
    "ICLFORGE_SENDSPIN*",
    "SPIRAM*",
    "ESP32S3_*CACHE*",
    "*IRAM_OPT*",
    "ESPTOOLPY_FLASHSIZE*",
    "ESPTOOLPY_FLASHMODE*",
    "PARTITION_TABLE_CUSTOM_FILENAME",
    "ESP32P4_*REV*",
    "ESP_DEFAULT_CPU_FREQ_MHZ_*",
    "BOOTLOADER_APP_ROLLBACK_ENABLE",
    "BOOTLOADER_LOG_LEVEL_*",
    "ESP_SYSTEM_ALLOW_RTC_FAST_MEM_AS_HEAP",
    "ESP_HOSTED_MEMPOOL_PREFER_SPIRAM",
    "ESP_COREDUMP_ENABLE_TO_*"
  ],
  "free": {
    "ICLFORGE_EXAMPLE_WIFI_*": "the board's network is its own, kept in NVS; a published image has none built in (package_firmware.py refuses one)",
    "ICLFORGE_EXAMPLE_HTTP_URL": "the stream a build plays at boot: empty on a board, a test server's on a CI shape",
    "ICLFORGE_EXAMPLE_PANEL_STACK_BYTES": "the screen task's stack, in PSRAM: declared for every target and inert in a profile whose panel is NONE (every one here); a profile that enables the screen locks it by hand, which verify honours before this",
    "LV_SPAN_SNIPPET_STACK_SIZE": "LVGL's own count of text-span snippets it keeps on its stack, not a task's stack: there on every P4 build, which carries the library, and used only where the screen is"
  },
  "other_stacks": {
    "sdkconfig.defaults;sdkconfig.ac4;sdkconfig.hw": "the bare-metal S3 probe's AC-4 build (firmware/baremetal), a footprint measurement and not the sink",
    "sdkconfig.defaults;sdkconfig.c6": "the C6 overlay's own header: the part with no Sendspin player, which no image is built for",
    "sdkconfig.defaults;sdkconfig.hw": "the S3 with neither PSRAM nor a network: the i2s_player example's shape, the bare-metal probe's and the README's first sections'; not a board's image",
    "sdkconfig.defaults;sdkconfig.hw;sdkconfig.p4": "the P4 overlay's own header: the part with no Sendspin player, which no image is built for",
    "sdkconfig.defaults;sdkconfig.hw;sdkconfig.p4;sdkconfig.p4-rev3;sdkconfig.sendspin": "sdkconfig.p4-rev3's own header: the v3.x revision over the P4 shape, before the panel; no image is built from it",
    "sdkconfig.defaults;sdkconfig.hw;sdkconfig.p4;sdkconfig.sendspin": "the P4 before the AC-4 decoder joined its release profile: the README's account of the first full Sendspin play on this part (2026-09); not a board's image",
    "sdkconfig.defaults;sdkconfig.hw;sdkconfig.p4;sdkconfig.sendspin;sdkconfig.panel;sdkconfig.panel-null": "the P4 with the panel's frame buffer in PSRAM and no screen behind it (sdkconfig.panel-null): what a board with no panel runs to see the screen; a development build, built and not run or packaged",
    "sdkconfig.defaults;sdkconfig.hw;sdkconfig.psram": "the S3 with PSRAM and a network before the Sendspin player: the HTTP-source shapes of the 714 and device-UI plans and the stream set; not a board's image",
    "sdkconfig.defaults;sdkconfig.wifi": "the bare-metal C6 probe's network load (firmware/baremetal), not the sink"
  },
  "overlays": {
    "wifi-credentials": {
      "touches": [
        "ICLFORGE_EXAMPLE_WIFI_*"
      ],
      "note": "a file of CONFIG_ICLFORGE_EXAMPLE_WIFI_SSID and _PASSWORD, given last, for a build that goes onto a bench board; never published"
    },
    "measure": {
      "touches": [
        "ICLFORGE_EXAMPLE_AC4_PCM_HASH",
        "ICLFORGE_EXAMPLE_REPORT_EVERY_FRAMES"
      ],
      "note": "observation only: the PCM hash an AC-4 play carries; no placement, size or cache. sdkconfig.measure sets ICLFORGE_EXAMPLE_AC4_PCM_HASH and nothing else; the report cadence is declared for a scratch build to change",
      "fragment": "measure"
    },
    "panel-capture": {
      "touches": [
        "ICLFORGE_EXAMPLE_PANEL_CAPTURE_PORT"
      ],
      "note": "the screen's read-back and touch server (HTTP on 8081, no authentication) on, for an image that is run on a bench: tools/hearth/screen_script.py drives a board's screen by it. A release profile locks the port at 0 and package_firmware.py refuses an image built with this overlay; sdkconfig.panel-capture sets that key and nothing else",
      "fragment": "panel-capture"
    },
    "qemu-net": {
      "touches": [
        "ICLFORGE_EXAMPLE_NETWORK_*",
        "ETH_USE_OPENETH",
        "ICLFORGE_EXAMPLE_SINK_*",
        "SPIRAM_MODE_*",
        "SPIRAM_SPEED*",
        "ESP_CONSOLE_*",
        "ESP_CONSOLE*"
      ],
      "fragment": "qemu-net",
      "note": "the release shape on QEMU (planning/esp32-platform-profiles.md): Ethernet in place of Wi-Fi, the capture sink in place of I2S, quad PSRAM in place of octal, the console on UART0; nothing about stacks, rings, caches or features"
    }
  },
